sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch06-25> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Although individual persistent structures in class 4 systems such as rule 110 behave fairly repetitively, collisions between them can produce cascades of new structures and outcomes that take very many steps to resolve, yielding behavior of immense complexity from an extremely simple rule.";
    dc:type "computational-observation";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Interactions among simple structures in rule 110 give immense complexity";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 6, “Starting from Randomness”; section “Structures in Class 4 Systems” (from p. 281), p. 291. Scope: rule 110 and other class 4 cellular automata"
}
